# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTHING DERIVED FROM THE GAME FILES GOES INTO GIT.
#
# Policy (see docs/licensing.md): decompilation and reverse engineering are done
# as a lawful user for interoperability (EU Software Directive 2009/24/EC Art. 6).
# The *results* stay on this machine. Committing extracted game data would
# redistribute it, which that exception does not cover — and a systematic
# extraction of the dat may additionally attract the sui generis database right
# (Directive 96/9/EC).
#
# Everything below is regenerateable from the user's own install.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The game itself — never tracked, ever.
/Age2HD/

# Generated game data: 1,166 units, 801 techs, 798 effects, 32 civs of extracted
# values. Reproduce with: cd tools && uv run python -m genconfig <dat> ../config
/config/gamedata/

# Derived artefacts: inflated dats, converted JSON dumps, probe output, Ghidra
# projects. 200+ MB of extracted content.
/build/

# Save games and recorded games are the player's own content; they may also embed
# map/unit state. Keep them local.
*.aoe2spgame
*.aoe2record
*.mgz
*.mgx

# Manifests carry hashes/counts of the excluded data. Harmless, but pointless
# without the files they describe, and it names the user's install.
/config/MANIFEST.toml

# Tooling virtualenvs and caches
tools/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
*.swp
